                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The passage seems choppy and disorganized because the topics of its sentences are inconsistent and diffuse. They do not focus our attention on a limited set of related ideas:",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                180,
                772,
                256
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 3,
            "global_group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    180.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    180.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    249.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    249.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": " $ \\underline{\\text{Consistent ideas toward the beginnings of sentences}} $, especially in their subjects, help readers understand what a passage is generally about.  $ \\underline{\\text{A sense of coherence}} $ arises when  $ \\underline{\\text{a sequence of topics}} $ comprises a narrow set of related ideas. But  $ \\underline{\\text{the context of each sentence}} $ is lost by seemingly random shifts of topics.  $ \\underline{\\text{Unfocused, even disorganized paragraphs}} $ result when  $ \\underline{\\text{that}} $ happens.",
            "block_bbox": [
                112,
                269,
                743,
                395
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    112.0,
                    269.0
                ],
                [
                    743.0,
                    269.0
                ],
                [
                    743.0,
                    395.0
                ],
                [
                    112.0,
                    395.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Now compare that passage to this revision, with the new topics boldfaced:",
            "block_bbox": [
                80,
                408,
                712,
                432
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    80.0,
                    408.0
                ],
                [
                    712.0,
                    408.0
                ],
                [
                    712.0,
                    432.0
                ],
                [
                    80.0,
                    432.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Readers understand what a passage is generally about when they see consistent ideas toward the beginnings of sentences, especially in their subjects. They feel a passage is coherent when they read a sequence of topics that focuses on a narrow set of related ideas. But when topics seem to shift randomly, readers lose the context of each sentence. When that happens, they feel they are reading paragraphs that are unfocused and even disorganized.",
            "block_bbox": [
                114,
                446,
                743,
                596
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    114.0,
                    446.0
                ],
                [
                    743.0,
                    446.0
                ],
                [
                    743.0,
                    596.0
                ],
                [
                    114.0,
                    596.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The subjects of sentences and clauses focus our attention on just two concepts—readers and topics—and form a strong topic string: readers, they, they, they, topics, readers, that, they [readers]. That is why this passage seems more coherent.",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                609,
                771,
                686
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    609.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    609.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    686.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    686.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "How to Revise: Cohesion and Coherence",
            "block_bbox": [
